# VCH Extension copy style

Applies to popup UI, VA.gov content-script messages, manifest description, and import consent copy.

## No em dashes

Do not use `—` or `–` as punctuation in user-facing copy.

Prefer periods, commas, colons, or parentheses. Use `-` or `N/A` for empty table cells, not an em dash.

## Avoid AI buzzword tone

Do not use hype words unless technically required: unlock (prefer "open", "view", "enable"), leverage, seamlessly, streamline, etc.

Prefer plain verbs: organize, use, help, may, sometimes, can, often.

## OK to keep

- Code comments and internal developer strings
- Function names like `unlock()` in passkey lock code (not shown verbatim to users)
